findings.claim:
Several details from the first draft are cut:
- 'a shade over average height… the impression of a big man';
- 'power and force';
- the actor-or-lawyer uncertainty;
- 'The great man had impressed her';
- 'He nodded as though she had answered'.
Only 'striking appearance' and 'Magnetism' remain.

Three things go:
- Boris's 'I believe you would sell your soul for money. I believe----', which builds to the broken 'sell-- _us!_' (kept in the first draft);
- the opening 'recklessness' line;
- Rita's 'Notoriety of the right kind' reply.
